value, is_regexp):\n\n        # Default value\n        result = dvalue\n\n        # Retrieve file section\n        try:\n            config = self.cp.items(section)\n        except configparser.NoSectionError:\n            raise AnsibleLookupError(\"Can't find section %s\" % section)\n\n        # Get the value of key or search the file with a regular expression\n        if is_regexp:\n            for option, value in config:\n                if re.match(key, option):\n                    result = value\n        elif key in dict(config):\n            result = config[config.index((key, dict(config)[key]))][1]\n\n        return result\n```\n\nHmm, and run():\n\n```python\n            try:\n                var = self.get_value(key, paramvals['section'], paramvals['default'], paramvals['re'])\n            except configparser.NoSectionError:\n                raise AnsibleLookupError(\"No section '{section}' in {file}\".format(section=paramvals['section'], file=paramvals['file']))\n```\n\nIf both are present, the run() except is unreachable. Hmm, but wait \u2014 maybe get_value does NOT have the try/except in the version matching the snippet. The snippet is from a specific version. The task extracted lines 138-204 of the file. The file version matters.\n\nOK \u2014 get_info('LookupModule.get_value') will resolve this definitively. Let me stop speculating.\n\nSimilarly get_info('_parse_params') resolves the parsing question.\n\nLet me also get_info('LookupBase') to see __init__ and confirm `_loader` attribute and `_deprecate_inline_kv` existence.\n\nAlright, let me make the calls now.\n\nAfter that, I'll finalize the test code.\n\nOne more design point: the task says \"Write as little top-level code as possible\" \u2014 so just imports, constants, helper, and test functions. No pytest.main.\n\nAlso \"Be sure to include assertions in the test that verify any applicable postconditions.\" \u2014 done via assert statements.\n\nAlso \"clean up after the test\" \u2014 tmp_path is