ne 167. Confirmed reachable. \n\nNow get_value:\n```python\ndef get_value(self, key, section, dflt, is_regexp):\n    if is_regexp:\n        return [v for k, v in self.cp.items(section) if re.match(key, k)]\n    value = None\n    try:\n        value = self.cp.get(section, key)\n    except configparser.NoOptionError:\n        return dflt\n    return value\n```\n\n- NoSectionError: `self.cp.items(section)` (regexp path) or `self.cp.get(section, key)` (normal path) raises NoSectionError \u2192 propagates \u2192 run's except \u2192 line 196-197. Reachable via either path. Use normal path: section='nope', key='key' \u2192 cp.get raises NoSectionError \u2192 run catches \u2192 AnsibleLookupError(\"No section 'nope' in ansible.ini\"). \n\n- NoOptionError \u2192 returns dflt. So missing key \u2192 default. var = dflt. If dflt None \u2192 var None \u2192 skip. Good.\n\n- regexp path returns a list \u2192 MutableSequence \u2192 lines 199-200. With matches: e.g. content '[global]\\nkey1 = v1\\nkey2 = v2\\n', term 'key.', re=True \u2192 cp.items('global') \u2192 [('key1','v1'),('key2','v2')] \u2192 re.match('key.', 'key1') \u2192 match \u2192 ['v1','v2'] \u2192 ret ['v1','v2']. \n\n  Note: with case_sensitive=False, optionxform lowercases \u2014 keys already lowercase. Good.\n\n  Also regexp with no matches \u2192 [] \u2192 var is [] (not None) \u2192 MutableSequence \u2192 loop over empty \u2192 ret []. Covers 198-True + 199-True with empty. Not needed separately.\n\n- allow_no_value: content '[global]\\nemptykey\\n' with allow_no_value=True \u2192 cp.get('global','emptykey') \u2192 returns None (value None). var = None \u2192 skip \u2192 ret []. Good \u2014 covers allow_no_value=True and var-None.\n\n  Wait \u2014 cp.get with allow_no_value: the option exists with value None \u2192 d[option] = None \u2192 returns None. Yes.\n\nNow, the properties test: type='properties' \u2192 config.write('[java_properties]\\n') then contents. Content 'key=javavalue\\n' \u2192 full stream '[java_properties]\\nkey=javavalue\\n' \u2192 section 'java_properties', option 'key' \u2192 'javavalue'. paramvals['section'] set to 'java_properties'. get_value('key','java_properties',None,False) \u2192 cp.get \u2192 'javavalue'. ret ['javavalue']. \n\nAlso assert that section was switched? Could check `lookup.cp` sections... not needed; the result assertion suffices (if section weren't switched, NoSectionError would be raised since 'global' doesn't exist in the properties content).\n\nNow the encoding test: content 'key = caf\u00e9\\n' encoded latin-1 \u2192 bytes b'key = caf\\xe9\\n'. to_text(..., encoding='latin-1') \u2192 'key = caf\u00e9\\n'. cp parses value 'caf\u00e9'. ret ['caf\u00e9']. If encoding were utf-8 (default), to_text would raise UnicodeDecodeError (surrogate_or_strict \u2192 strict on py3). So the test verifies encoding is honored. \n\nNow \u2014 one more check on `to_text(contents, errors='surrogate_or_strict', encoding=paramvals['encoding'])`: `surrogate_or_strict` on Python 3 \u2192 'strict'. Good.\n\nNow, the DuplicateOptionError test: content '[global]\\nkey = a\\nkey = b\\n' \u2192 readfp raises DuplicateOptionError \u2192 line 191-192 \u2192 AnsibleLookupError(\"Duplicate option in 'ansible.ini': ...\"). Match 'Duplicate option'. \n\nHmm \u2014 one caveat: DuplicateOptionError message: \"Duplicate option in: ...\" hmm, the configparser message is like \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\"? Actually DuplicateOptionError message format: `DuplicateOptionError` is raised with source/lineno/option/section \u2014 the str is built by ParsingError.format... e.g. \"File \\\"<unknown>\\\", line 2: option 'key' already exists\" hmm. Actually:\n\n```\nDuplicateOptionError: while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\n```\n\nHmm, in Python 3: `e.message` = \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\"? Let me think \u2014 ParsingError.formatmessage: `'%s:' % self.source` + ... For DuplicateOptionError, the message is \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\"? I believe str(e) gives something like \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\". Hmm, actually I recall: `DuplicateOptionError: while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists`. Hmm, or \"File \\\"<string>\\\", line 2\"... The `source` is None for readfp(StringIO) \u2192 formatmessage: if source is None \u2192 \"while parsing from stream\" hmm... Actually ParsingError.formatmessage:\n\n```python\ndef formatmessage(self):\n    if self.source is None:\n        return \"while parsing from stream\"\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm no:\n\n```python\ndef formatmessage(self):\n    if self.source is None:\n        return \"while parsing from stream\"\n    else:\n        return \"while parsing from %s\" % self.source\n```\n\nHmm, not exactly, but close. The full message: \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\"? Something like that. Anyway, my match 'Duplicate option' \u2014 wait, does the message contain \"Duplicate option\"? NO! The exception CLASS is DuplicateOptionError but the MESSAGE doesn't contain \"Duplicate option\". The message is like \"while parsing from stream: option 'key' in section 'global' already exists\".\n\nBut the AnsibleLookupError message is: \"Duplicate option in '{file}': {error}\".format(...) \u2192 \"Duplicate option in 'ansible.ini': while parsing...\". So the raised AnsibleLookupError message DOES contain \"Duplicate option\". My match='Duplicate option' matches the AnsibleLookupError message. \n\nNow, pytest.raises match uses re.search on the string representation. AnsibleLookupError str \u2014 AnsibleError.__str__ returns the message (possibly with orig_exc appended). Fine.\n\nNow, about `match=\"No section 'nope'\"` \u2014 the message: \"No section 'nope' in ansible.ini\". re.search with that pattern \u2014 