nNow, where to put the shim? In `_make_lookup`, before creating... actually the ConfigParser instance is created inside run(), so patching the class any time before run() is fine. Put it at the top of the helper.\n\nAlso \u2014 the import in the test: `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves import configparser` \u2014 to guarantee we patch the exact module object the plugin uses. On py3 this is the stdlib module. \u2713.\n\nHmm \u2014 one concern: `six.moves.configparser` is a lazy module loader; `from ansible.module_utils.six.moves import configparser` gives the stdlib configparser module object. `configparser.ConfigParser` \u2014 same class as plugin's. \u2713.\n\nNow, let me also re-examine: after fixing readfp, will `test_set_options_receives_variables_and_direct_kwargs` pass fully? run: set_options recorded {'var_options': {'x':1}, 'direct': {}}. get_options \u2192 params. cp created. term 'key' \u2014 no '=' no ' ' \u2192 skip inline. find_file \u2192 path. StringIO. type 'ini'. contents from loader mock: BASIC_INI encoded utf-8. to_text \u2192 str. write. seek. read_file shim \u2192 parses [global] key=value, other=ovalue, [other_section] key=ovalue2. get_value('key','global',None,False) \u2192 cp.get('global','key') \u2192 'value'. var='value' \u2192 not None \u2192 not MutableSequence \u2192 ret ['value']. \u2713. Assertion `== ['value']` \u2713. recorded assertion \u2713.\n\nAll other tests should now pass. Let me re-verify a few tricky ones with the shim in place:\n\n- `test_duplicate_option_is_reported`: read_file raises DuplicateOptionError \u2192 caught \u2192 AnsibleLookupError(\"Duplicate option in 'ansible.ini': ...\"). match 'Duplicate option' \u2713.\n\n- `test_missing_section_is_reported`: get_value \u2192 cp.get('nope','key') \u2192 NoSectionError \u2192 propagates \u2192 run catches \u2192 \"No section 'nope' in ansible.ini\" \u2713.\n\n- `test_properties_type_uses_synthetic_java_properties_section`: config = '[java_properties]\\n' + 'key=javavalue\\n' \u2192 parses. cp.get('java_properties','key') \u2192 'javavalue' \u2713.\n\n- `test_allow_no_value_accepts_valueless_entries`: allow_no_value=True \u2192 'emptykey' parses with None value. cp.get('global','emptykey') \u2192 None \u2192 var None \u2192 ret [] \u2713.\n\n- `test_encoding_option_is_honoured`: content.encode('latin-1') \u2192 to_text latin-1 \u2192 'caf\u00e9' \u2713.\n\n- `test_inline_value_with_extra_equals_is_rejected`: 'key=a=b' \u2192 _parse_params \u2192 ['key=a=b'] \u2192 split('=') \u2192 ValueError \u2192 AnsibleLookupError \"Could not use 'key=a=b' from ...\" \u2713.\n\nWait \u2014 double-check _parse_params for 'key=a=b' once more with the real code:\n\n```python\ndef _parse_params(term, paramvals):\n    valid_keys = paramvals.keys()\n    params = defaultdict(lambda: '')\n    keys = []\n    thiskey = 'key'\n    for idp, phrase in enumerate(term.split()):\n        if '=' in phrase:\n            for k in valid_keys:\n                if '%s=' % k in phrase:\n                    thiskey = k\n        if idp == 0 or not params[thiskey]:\n            params[thiskey] = phrase\n            keys.append(thiskey)\n        else:\n            params[thiskey] += ' ' + phrase\n    return [params[x] for x in keys]\n```\n\nterm 'key=a=b' \u2192 split() \u2192 ['key=a=b']. idp=0: '=' in phrase \u2192 loop valid_keys: any '%s=' % k in 'key=a=b'? valid keys: file, section, default, re, type, encoding, case_sensitive, allow_no_value. 'file=' no, 'section=' no, 'default=' no, 're=' no, 'type=' no, 'encoding=' no, 'case_sensitive=' no, 'allow_no_value=' no. thiskey stays 'key'. idp==0 \u2192 params['key']='key=a=b'. Return ['key=a=b']. \u2713 \u2192 run: split('=') \u2192 3 parts \u2192 ValueError \u2713.\n\n- `test_inline_unknown_option_is_rejected` term 'bogus=1': idp=0, '=' in phrase \u2192 valid_keys loop: none match ('bogus=' not a valid key prefix; check 're=' in 'bogus=1'? no). thiskey='key'. params['key']='bogus=1'. Return ['bogus=1']. run: split('=')