ms including DEFAULT section entries. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `configparser` lowercases keys by default (optionxform). Values preserved.\n\nNow write the test script:\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom ansible.module_utils.six.moves import StringIO, configparser\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ansible.plugins.lookup.ini import LookupModule\n\n\nINI_DATA = \"\"\"\n[products]\nmod_version = 1.0\nmod_name = hammer\ntool_version = 2.0\n\"\"\"\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef lookup():\n    lm = LookupModule()\n    cp = configparser.ConfigParser()\n    cp.read_file(StringIO(INI_DATA))\n    lm.cp = cp\n    return lm\n\n\ndef test_get_value_single_existing(lookup):\n    \"\"\"is_regexp False, option exists -> value returned (lines 128, 130-131, 134).\"\"\"\n    assert lookup.get_value('mod_name', 'products', None, False) == 'hammer'\n\n\ndef test_get_value_missing_option_returns_default(lookup):\n    \"\"\"is_regexp False, option missing -> NoOptionError path returns dflt (lines 132-133).\"\"\"\n    sentinel = object()\n    assert lookup.get_value('nope', 'products', sentinel, False) is sentinel\n\n\ndef test_get_value_regexp_matches(lookup):\n    \"\"\"is_regexp True -> list of values whose keys match (lines 126-127).\"\"\"\n    res = lookup.get_value(r'.*_version$', 'products', None, True)\n    assert sorted(res) == ['1.0', '2.0']\n\n\ndef test_get_value_regexp_no_match(lookup):\n    res = lookup.get_value(r'^zzz', 'products', None, True)\n    assert res == []\n```\n\nWait \u2014 does `LookupModule()` constructor work? Need to verify. In ansible-core, `AnsiblePlugin.__init__`:\n\nLooking at ansible-core 2.15 lib/ansible/plugins/__init__.py:\n\n```python\nclass AnsiblePlugin(object):\n\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n\n        self._options = {}\n\n        try:\n            self._name = kwargs.pop('_name')\n        except (KeyError, AttributeError):\n            self._name = None\n\n        self._tempvars = kwargs.get('tempvars', {})\n     